# Who can nod in this repository: the trust root (nod ADR 0002).
#
# One line per key, in OpenSSH's allowed_signers format:
#   <github-login> namespaces="nod" <key-type> <public-key> [comment]
# The principal is the GitHub login, exactly as GitHub spells it. A nod by the
# PR's author counts as "self", a nod by anyone else listed here as "peer".
#
# The verifier reads this file from the default branch on every run, so:
# - it may be empty: GitHub approvals still count, only what needs a signed nod
#   (changes under .nod/ and .github/workflows/, rules with approvals: false)
#   waits until someone is enrolled;
# - adding a key is a PR to this file; it is under .nod/, so a peer must nod it
#   (the first one, with nobody to nod it, merges the usual way while the nod
#   check is not required);
# - removing a key revokes that key's nods on every open PR at the next run;
# - `valid-after="20270101"` / `valid-before="…"` options help rotate a key.
